    <string name="aa_opacity_floor_hint">0% is stored as given. Text surfaces render at their readability floor instead: input and chat dock 35%, cards 18%, sidebar 45%, drawer 65%, detail and quota panels 62%. Static menus, dialogs and sheets composite over the window background; at 0% they show that backing color, not transparency.</string>
    <string name="aa_blur_radius_hint">0 dp means no blur, but a live liquid-glass surface can still sample for refraction. Android 12–12L caps live blur at 12 dp, Android 13+ up to 40 dp; older versions keep the value without blur.</string>
    <string name="aa_refraction_hint">Refraction is independent of blur radius: it needs Android 13+, the automatic or AGSL renderer, a live source and enabled effects; it can still bend the backdrop at 0 dp blur.</string>
    <string name="aa_topbar_capsule_hint">The top bar capsule keeps using this toggle and radius even when Show top bar background is off.</string>
    <string name="aa_solid_hint">Solid doesn’t sample the background, so the opacity and blur rows are skipped.</string>
    <string name="aa_bubble_inherit_hint">The surface opacity and radius apply when no role-specific override is set. Explicit frosted alpha and blur override those values on blur-capable materials; solid bubbles never blur.</string>
    <string name="aa_glass_style_hint">Applies to every liquid glass surface: input, top bar, cards, overlays, sidebar, dock, bubbles and rich content. Salt is the default; the original keeps RikkaHub’s fixed optics and ignores the Salt sliders.</string>
    <string name="aa_adaptive_hint">While the list is scrolling, the keyboard is open, a reply is generating, or the device is in battery saver, live sampling pauses; the material keeps the stored opacity.</string>
